#!/bin/sh
# vms: the machine's shared virtual machines, in $COWORKER_HOME/vms (COWORKER_HOME is ~/coworker
# unless set), used by one project at a time. README.md, "VMs".
#
#   vms claim   VM PROJECT                                PROJECT needs VM
#   vms release VM PROJECT                                PROJECT is done with VM (never deletes it)
#   vms run     VM DIR [--keep-vm] [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...]
#                                                         the one call: claim VM with DIR's needs of
#                                                         it, merge every claimant's, lock, start it
#                                                         if it's down, check it, run COMMAND, stop it
#                                                         if this run started it
#   vms lock    VM PROJECT [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...]  run COMMAND holding VM's lock
#   vms env     VM                                        how to reach VM, as assignments to eval
#   vms list                                              every VM, its claims, and who holds it
#
# Beside each VM's folder (its README.md and vm.env): an empty VM.<project> per project that claims
# it, and VM.lock, which names the holder while a run holds it.
set -eu
DIR=${COWORKER_HOME:-$HOME/coworker}/vms
USAGE="usage: vms run VM DIR [--keep-vm] [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...] | claim VM PROJECT | release VM PROJECT | lock VM PROJECT [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...] | env VM | list"
DEPS="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)/deps"
usage() { echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2; }

project() {     # project NAME: exit 2 unless NAME can be a project's name
    case $1 in ''|*[!A-Za-z0-9_-]*|lock) echo "vms: a project name is letters, digits, - and _ (and isn't lock)" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
}
client() {      # the installed half of the handshake: a call that changes shared state comes through a
                # project's coworker submodule, which passes its protocol (README.md, "Protocol"); exit 3
    mine=$(cat "$(dirname "$0")/../PROTOCOL" 2>/dev/null || true)
    c=${COWORKER_CLIENT_PROTOCOL:-}
    if [ -z "$c" ]; then
        echo "vms: called directly, not through a project's coworker submodule: a project calls <its checkout>/coworker/bin/vms (coworker ${mine:-?}; README.md, \"In a project\")" >&2
        exit 3
    fi
    case $c.$mine in *[!0-9.]*|*..*) echo "vms: can't read the protocols (this project's '$c', installed '$mine')" >&2; exit 3 ;; esac
    if [ "${c%%.*}" != "${mine%%.*}" ] || [ "${mine#*.}" -lt "${c#*.}" ]; then
        echo "vms: this project's coworker is protocol $c and the installed one is $mine: the machine's owner moves them together (README.md, \"Protocol\")" >&2
        exit 3
    fi
}

claims_of() {   # claims_of VM: the projects that claim VM, each after a space
    out=""
    for f in "$DIR/$1".*; do
        [ -f "$f" ] || continue
        s=${f#"$DIR/$1".}
        case $s in *.*|lock) ;; *) out="$out $s" ;; esac
    done
    echo "$out"
}

claim() {
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); P=$2
    project "$P"
    mkdir -p "$DIR"
    touch "$DIR/$VM.$P"
    if [ -f "$DIR/$VM/vm.env" ]; then echo "$P claims $VM"; else echo "$P claims $VM, not set up yet: no $DIR/$VM/vm.env"; fi
}

release() {     # a VM is never deleted by a script: with the last claim gone this says so, and the owner decides
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); P=$2
    rm -f "$DIR/$VM.$P"
    left=$(claims_of "$VM")
    if [ -z "$left" ]; then
        echo "$P released $VM; no project claims it now: ask the machine's owner before deleting $DIR/$VM"
    else
        echo "$P released $VM; kept, claimed by$left"
    fi
}

lock() {        # COMMAND sees COWORKER_VM_LOCKED=<vm>; --no-wait exits 75 when another run holds it
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); P=$2
    shift 2
    WAIT=1
    [ "${1:-}" = --no-wait ] && { WAIT=0; shift; }
    [ "${1:-}" = -- ] || { echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2; }
    shift
    [ $# -gt 0 ] || { echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2; }
    [ -d "$DIR/$VM" ] || { echo "vms: no VM $VM in $DIR" >&2; exit 1; }
    L="$DIR/$VM.lock"
    exec 9>>"$L"
    if ! flock -n 9; then
        who=$(cat "$L" 2>/dev/null || true)
        [ "$WAIT" = 1 ] || { echo "$VM is in use: ${who:-by another run}" >&2; exit 75; }
        echo "$VM is in use: ${who:-by another run}; waiting for it"
        flock 9
    fi
    printf '%s, pid %s, since %s\n' "$P" "$$" "$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z')" > "$L"
    COWORKER_VM_LOCKED=$VM
    export COWORKER_VM_LOCKED
    rc=0
    "$@" || rc=$?
    : > "$L"
    exit "$rc"
}

env_of() {      # VM_HOME and each VM_* setting in vm.env, with the key and known-hosts paths made absolute
    [ $# -ge 1 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1")
    H="$DIR/$VM"
    [ -f "$H/vm.env" ] || { echo "vms: no $H/vm.env (README.md, \"vm.env\")" >&2; exit 1; }
    H=$(cd "$H" && pwd -P)
    q() { printf "'%s'" "$(printf '%s' "$1" | sed "s/'/'\\\\''/g")"; }
    (
        unset VM_OS VM_CONTAINER VM_SSH_HOST VM_SSH_PORT VM_SSH_USER VM_SSH_KEY VM_KNOWN_HOSTS
        . "$H/vm.env"
        for k in VM_SSH_PORT VM_SSH_USER VM_SSH_KEY; do
            eval "v=\${$k:-}"
            [ -n "$v" ] || { echo "vms: $H/vm.env sets no $k" >&2; exit 1; }
        done
        abs() { case $1 in /*) printf '%s' "$1" ;; ?*) printf '%s/%s' "$H" "$1" ;; esac; }
        echo "VM_HOME=$(q "$H")"
        echo "VM_OS=$(q "${VM_OS:-}")"
        echo "VM_CONTAINER=$(q "${VM_CONTAINER:-}")"
        echo "VM_SSH_HOST=$(q "${VM_SSH_HOST:-127.0.0.1}")"
        echo "VM_SSH_PORT=$(q "$VM_SSH_PORT")"
        echo "VM_SSH_USER=$(q "$VM_SSH_USER")"
        echo "VM_SSH_KEY=$(q "$(abs "$VM_SSH_KEY")")"
        echo "VM_KNOWN_HOSTS=$(q "$(abs "${VM_KNOWN_HOSTS:-known_hosts}")")"
    )
}

run_() {         # exit: 1 the host lacks a need (deps install), 65 the projects' needs clash,
                # 69 the VM doesn't meet them (or won't start), 75 busy with --no-wait; else COMMAND's
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); D=$2
    shift 2
    KEEP=0; NOWAIT=""
    while :; do
        case ${1:-} in
            --keep-vm) KEEP=1; shift ;;
            --no-wait) NOWAIT=--no-wait; shift ;;
            --) shift; break ;;
            *) usage ;;
        esac
    done
    [ $# -gt 0 ] || usage
    [ -f "$D/.coworker/deps.json" ] || { echo "vms: no $D/.coworker/deps.json (README.md, \"Dependencies\")" >&2; exit 2; }
    P=$(basename "$(cd "$D" && pwd -P)")  # a project's name is its checkout directory's (the real one)
    "$DEPS" vm-claim "$VM" "$D" || exit $?
    lock "$VM" "$P" $NOWAIT -- run_locked "$@"
}

run_locked() {  # under the lock: start the VM if it's down, check it, COMMAND, stop it if started here
    eval "$(env_of "$VM")"
    export VM_HOME VM_OS VM_CONTAINER VM_SSH_HOST VM_SSH_PORT VM_SSH_USER VM_SSH_KEY VM_KNOWN_HOSTS
    STARTED=0
    if [ -n "$VM_CONTAINER" ] && [ "$(docker inspect -f '{{.State.Running}}' "$VM_CONTAINER" 2>/dev/null)" != true ]; then
        echo "starting $VM ($VM_CONTAINER)"
        docker start "$VM_CONTAINER" >/dev/null || { echo "vms: couldn't start $VM_CONTAINER" >&2; return 69; }
        STARTED=1
        trap 'stop_started; exit 130' INT TERM HUP
    fi
    rc=0
    "$DEPS" vm-guest "$VM" --wait "${COWORKER_VM_BOOT_WAIT:-900}" || rc=$?
    [ "$rc" = 0 ] && { "$@" || rc=$?; }
    stop_started
    return "$rc"
}

stop_started() {
    [ "$STARTED" = 1 ] || return 0
    STARTED=0
    if [ "$KEEP" = 1 ]; then
        echo "$VM left running (--keep-vm): stopping it is $P's"
    else
        echo "stopping $VM (this run started it)"
        docker stop -t 120 "$VM_CONTAINER" >/dev/null || echo "vms: couldn't stop $VM_CONTAINER" >&2
    fi
}

list() {
    [ -d "$DIR" ] || { echo "no $DIR"; return 0; }
    cd "$DIR"
    names=$({ for f in *; do [ -d "$f" ] && echo "$f"; done
              for f in *.*; do [ -f "$f" ] || continue; s=${f##*.}
                  [ "$s" = lock ] || echo "${f%."$s"}"; done; } | sort -u)
    for v in $names; do
        c=$(claims_of "$v")
        if [ -f "$v/vm.env" ]; then what=$( (. "./$v/vm.env"; echo "${VM_OS:-a VM}") )
        else what="not set up yet (no $v/vm.env)"; fi
        use=free
        if [ -e "$v.lock" ] && ! ( flock -n 9 ) 9>>"$v.lock"; then use="in use: $(cat "$v.lock")"; fi
        if [ -n "$c" ]; then echo "$v | $what | claimed by$c | $use"; else echo "$v | $what | unclaimed | $use"; fi
    done
}

cmd=${1:-}
[ $# -gt 0 ] && shift
case $cmd in
    run) client; run_ "$@" ;;
    claim) client; claim "$@" ;;
    release) client; release "$@" ;;
    lock) client; lock "$@" ;;
    env) env_of "$@" ;;
    list) list ;;
    *) echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
